Yang Bai received his Ph.D. degree in Inorganic Chemistry from Nanjing University in 2018. Then he joined Prof. Huan Pang's group as a postdoctoral fellow in Yangzhou University. His research is focused on MOF-based functional nanomaterials for multiple applications.
Chao Yu received his Ph.D. degree in Materials-Oriented Chemical Engineering at Nanjing University of Technology in 2014 under the supervision of Prof. Su Chen, and then joined Prof. Shouheng Sun's group at Brown University as a postdoctoral research associate. He is now a Professor of Chemistry and Engineering at Jiangsu University of Science and Technology. His research interest is on developing new assembly methods of nanomaterials and their application for greener heterogeneous catalysts.
Huan Pang received his Ph.D. degree from Nanjing University in 2011. He is now a university distinguished professor at Yangzhou University and Young Changjiang Scholars of the Ministry of Education. He is a senior member of the China Chemical Association. He is the managing editor of EnergyChem, the editorial board member of FlatChem and Rare Metals, and the youth editorial board member of e-Science, Advanced Fiber Materials, Chinese Journal of Inorganic Chemistry, and China Chemical Letters. He was recognized as a highly cited researcher in Cross-Field by Clarivate Analytics in 2020.
